    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="8" relname="preparation">I agree with you when you say that the majority of users will never become information technology specialists.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="8" relname="span">It's funny how the new trend in marketing for many coorporation is targeted towards the tech-savy generation.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="10" relname="span">Those users who are from a non tech savvy world are often puzzled</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="3" relname="nonvolitional-cause">as they do not know how to use many applications.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="11" relname="span">Many applications are apparently not intuitive to many users.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="evidence">Applications for Banking sites (as in your example) are good examples of sites that need a extra pinch of intutiveness built in for the novice user.</segment>
        <group id="7" type="span"/>
        <group id="8" type="span" parent="7" relname="span"/>
        <group id="9" type="span" parent="2" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="elaboration"/>
    </body>
